.TH SSHADY 1 "June 2026" "sshady 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sshady \- manage SSH proxy configurations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshady
[\fIglobal-flags\fR]
.br
.B sshady create
[\fI--alias\fR \fIname\fR] [\fI--host\fR \fIaddr\fR] [\fI--user\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fI--port\fR \fIport\fR] [\fI--identity-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fI--proxy-type\fR \fItype\fR] [\fI--proxy-host\fR \fIaddr\fR]
[\fI--proxy-port\fR \fIport\fR] [\fI--proxy-user\fR \fIuser\fR]
[\fI--proxy-pass\fR \fIpass\fR] [\fI--proxy-pass-file\fR \fIpath\fR]
[\fI--jump-host\fR \fIuser@host\fR]
.br
.B sshady list
.br
.B sshady show
\fIalias\fR
.br
.B sshady validate
[\fI--all\fR] [\fI--test-proxy\fR] [\fIalias\fR]
.br
.B sshady test
[\fI--timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR] \fIalias\fR
.br
.B sshady delete
\fIalias\fR
.br
.B sshady completion
\fIbash|zsh|fish|powershell\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBsshady\fR generates SSH proxy configuration blocks and writes them
to \fB~/.ssh/config\fR. It supports SOCKS4, SOCKS4a, SOCKS5, HTTP CONNECT,
Tor, and SSH jump host proxies.
.P
Running \fBsshady\fR with no arguments launches an interactive wizard.
All subcommands can also be used non-interactively via flags.
.P
Entries written by sshady are wrapped in BEGIN/END marker comments
so they can be tracked, listed, and removed by sshady without
affecting other SSH configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global Flags
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIpath\fR
Use an alternative SSH config file (default: \fI~/.ssh/config\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Preview changes without writing to the config file.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing sshady-managed entries without prompting.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR, \fB\-v\fR
Enable verbose diagnostic output.
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR, \fB\-q\fR
Suppress non-error output (useful for scripting).
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Print help and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS create
Create a new proxy configuration entry. Without flags, launches an
interactive wizard.
.TP
\fB\-\-alias\fR \fIname\fR
SSH host alias (required). Must match \fB^[a\-zA\-Z0\-9][a\-zA\-Z0\-9._\-]*$\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR \fIaddr\fR
Target hostname or IP address (required).
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fIuser\fR
SSH user (default: current OS user or \fB$USER\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fIport\fR
SSH port (default: 22).
.TP
\fB\-\-identity\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
Path to SSH private key.
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-type\fR \fItype\fR
Proxy type. One of: \fBsocks4\fR, \fBsocks4a\fR, \fBsocks5\fR, \fBhttp\fR, \fBtor\fR, \fBjump\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-host\fR \fIaddr\fR
Proxy hostname or IP (required for socks4/socks4a/socks5/http).
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-port\fR \fIport\fR
Proxy port (default: 1080).
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-user\fR \fIuser\fR
Proxy authentication username.
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-pass\fR \fIpass\fR
Proxy password. WARNING: visible in \fBps aux\fR. Prefer \fB\-\-proxy\-pass\-file\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-pass\-file\fR \fIpath\fR
Read proxy password from file. First line is used, trailing whitespace trimmed.
.TP
\fB\-\-jump\-host\fR \fIuser@host\fR
Jump host for \fB\-\-proxy\-type jump\fR.
.SS list
List all entries managed by sshady. Shows alias, target host, proxy type,
and authentication status.
.SS show
Display detailed information for a specific entry, including the
full SSH config block that would be written.
.SS validate
Validate an entry (or all entries with \fB\-\-all\fR).
Runs \fBssh \-G\fR to check SSH config syntax, then optionally tests
proxy reachability with \fB\-\-test\-proxy\fR.
.SS test
Test proxy TCP reachability using \fBncat \-z\fR. Exits 0 if reachable,
non-zero otherwise.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR
Connection timeout in seconds (default: 5, minimum: 1).
.SS delete
Remove an sshady-managed entry from the SSH config. A timestamped
backup is automatically created before removal.
.SS completion
Generate shell completion script for the specified shell.
.P
.B bash:
.RS
source <(sshady completion bash)
.RE
.P
.B zsh:
.RS
source <(sshady completion zsh)
.RE
.P
.B fish:
.RS
sshady completion fish | source
.RE
.P
.B powershell:
.RS
sshady completion powershell | Out\-String | Invoke\-Expression
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBSSHADY_CONFIG\fR
Override the default SSH config path. Equivalent to \fB\-\-config\fR.
.TP
\fBSSHADY_HOME\fR
Override the home directory used for path resolution.
.TP
\fBSSHADY_PROXY_PASS\fR
Proxy password (avoids \fB\-\-proxy\-pass\fR appearing in process list).
.TP
\fBSSH_ASKPASS\fR
If set, sshady respects the SSH askpass program for key prompts.
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
If set, disable colored output.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.ssh/config\fR
SSH client configuration file. sshady reads and writes managed blocks here.
Permissions are enforced to \fB0600\fR.
.TP
\fI~/.ssh/config.sshady.*.bak\fR
Timestamped backup files (last 5 retained). Format:
\fIconfig.sshady.YYYYMMDD\-HHMMSS.bak\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
Success.
.TP
\fB1\fR
General error (invalid arguments, config issues).
.TP
\fB2\fR
Proxy unreachable (test/validate --test-proxy).
.TP
\fB3\fR
SSH config syntax error (validate).
.TP
\fB4\fR
Missing prerequisites (ncat not found, etc.).
.TP
\fB5\fR
Interrupted by user.
.SH SECURITY
.P
\fBsshady\fR writes proxy credentials to \fB~/.ssh/config\fR with
\fB0600\fR permissions. To minimize exposure:
.IP \(bu 3
Use \fB\-\-proxy\-pass\-file\fR or \fBSSHADY_PROXY_PASS\fR instead of
\fB\-\-proxy\-pass\fR (which is visible in \fBps aux\fR).
.IP \(bu
Ensure \fB~/.ssh/\fR has \fB0700\fR permissions and \fB~/.ssh/config\fR
has \fB0600\fR (sshady enforces this automatically).
.IP \(bu
SOCKS4/SOCKS4a proxies do not support authentication. Use SOCKS5
with credentials if authentication is required.
.IP \(bu
The \fBtest\fR command establishes a TCP connection to the proxy.
The proxy operator can see this connection.
.IP \(bu
All input values (hostnames, ports, aliases, credentials) are
validated to prevent command injection and SSH config injection.
.P
For vulnerability reporting, see \fBSECURITY.md\fR in the project
repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBssh\fR(1),
\fBssh_config\fR(5),
\fBssh\-agent\fR(1),
\fBnc\fR(1),
\fBncat\fR(1),
\fBcurl\fR(1)
.P
Project repository: \fIhttps://github.com/Miro\-sh/sshady\fR
